WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.977
Paradev goes fully

00:00:01.789 --> 00:00:02.920
open source again

00:00:03.438 --> 00:00:05.501
Paradev formerly Superset

00:00:05.702 --> 00:00:06.327
moved to a

00:00:06.138 --> 00:00:07.671
more restrictive license

00:00:07.483 --> 00:00:08.473
in February

00:00:08.612 --> 00:00:09.520
Now the team

00:00:09.331 --> 00:00:10.345
has switched back

00:00:10.157 --> 00:00:11.064
to MIT

00:00:11.590 --> 00:00:12.144
It is a

00:00:11.956 --> 00:00:13.040
desktop app for

00:00:12.852 --> 00:00:14.078
running coding agents

00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:14.950
like Claude Code

00:00:14.762 --> 00:00:15.729
and Codex in

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:16.295
parallel

00:00:16.566 --> 00:00:17.191
each in its

00:00:17.026 --> 00:00:18.158
own Git worktree

00:00:18.686 --> 00:00:19.723
The team invites

00:00:19.629 --> 00:00:20.572
anyone to fork

00:00:20.384 --> 00:00:21.268
it or build

00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:21.976
their own product

00:00:21.787 --> 00:00:22.329
on it

00:00:22.469 --> 00:00:23.706
Its GitHub repo

00:00:23.518 --> 00:00:24.390
has more than

00:00:24.202 --> 00:00:25.794
16,000 stars

00:00:26.334 --> 00:00:27.348
Full story on

00:00:27.159 --> 00:00:28.055
the dashboard
